"""Translate the raft-ui design-system CSS into Flutter design tokens.

Source of truth (vendored, hashed in tool/design-source/manifest.json):
  raft-ui 0.5.27 dist/foundation.css   raw ramps + theme blocks (brutal, elegant, elegant.dark)
  raft-ui 0.5.27 dist/styles.css       Tailwind @theme aliases (black/white, brutal bare aliases, ease)
  raft-ui 0.5.27 dist/fonts.css        per-theme font stacks
  tailwindcss 4.2.2 theme.css          default scale (spacing, radius, text, weights, ...)
  raft-source 26f77ef web index.css    product @theme overrides (+ :root.dark code colours)

Output: packages/raft_ui/lib/src/tokens/*.g.dart (GENERATED — do not edit).

Usage:
  tool/gen-tokens                 regenerate Dart
  tool/gen-tokens --check         exit 1 if the generated Dart is stale
  tool/gen-tokens --oracle        compare against docs/theme-tokens/*.json (browser readback)
  tool/gen-tokens --import-sources --raft-ui DIR --raft-source DIR [--tailwind DIR]
                                  refresh the vendored CSS copies and manifest hashes

Stdlib only. The colour pipeline follows CSS Color 4 + Chrome:
  oklch -> OKLab -> LMS (cubed) -> XYZ-D65 -> linear sRGB (unclamped)
  color-mix(in srgb-linear, ...) interpolates premultiplied in linear sRGB (unclamped)
  final paint: gamma-encode (sign preserving), clip each channel to [0, 1], round to 8 bits.
Chrome does not apply the CSS Color 4 chroma-reduction gamut map when painting;
it clips per channel, which is what this file does (verified against the oracle).
Alpha is carried exactly (oklch(... / 0.1) emits opacity 0.1, never 26/255).
"""
